## 4. Observed Defects / Blockers

| ID | Severity | Component | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `QA-0042` (hypothetical) | S1 (critical) | `scoring/evidence.py` | Two-token acronym overlap (`ai/ml`) produces false positive `m = 0.4675` against unrelated phrases (`AI governance`). Fix: tighten threshold for short targets. |
| `QA-0031` (hypothetical) | S2 (major) | `scoring/evidence.py` | Keyword fallback scans only structured skills (`skills_evidenced`), not full resume text. Many preferred skills (e.g., `security`, `tunneling`) are missed when they appear only in experience bullets. Fix: full-text scanner in structurer. |
| `QA-0015` (hypothetical) | S8 (major) | `scoring/dimensions/s8_skill_recency.py` | S8 selects the three highest-weighted required skills, including missing ones (`Go` with weight 4), giving `S8 = 33.33`. Changing S8 to average only matched skills would improve the score for candidates who lack low-frequency high-weight skills. The external report’s S8 is likely computed differently. |
| QG3 | S1 (release blocker) | `tests/` | Q-PERF 1,000-resume performance benchmark not executed; Q-GOLD accuracy benchmark not verified; `docs/runbook.md` not executed from a clean machine; Legal fairness dossier not signed. Per `docs/QA_PLAN.md`, these block QG3. |

---

## 5. Recommendation

The code is **correct and clean** for the current Wave-1 + partial Wave-2 scope. The remaining work to reach the external report scores is **not a bug fix**; it is a **methodological divergence** between the frozen TRD ten-dimension model and the external rubric (weighted keyword coverage + minimum-qualification gate + role-expectation terms). The three algorithmic fixes above (keyword overlap threshold, full-text scanner, minimum-qualification gate) will bring the local scores closer to the external reports without violating the TRD contracts. They can all be implemented within the component boundaries defined in `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` (§2.2).

Proceed with the three high-priority fixes, run `make gate`, and re-run the full pipeline on `TESTDATA/deepak_ayushi` before deciding whether a separate external-rubric lens is needed.